IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il43-nouns`
IMPORT `il43-cross-references`

-- Row il-43. The sound citations point at what their citing words say, and the recorded facts about the defect and the controls are what NOTES.md says they are.
-- The defect itself is NOT asserted sound anywhere in this file: its two failing assertions are in il43-tests-xrefs-red.l4.
-- Every expected value is written from the texts quoted in il43-cross-references.l4, not from the output of the module.

§ `Tests of the sound citations`

-- The three controls point at what they say.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 1יג(ד)(2) to NII s 1, the retirement age`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 1יג(ד)(2) to NII s 223, the nursing benefit`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 2(א1)(1) to NII s 398(א2)(5), a person with a determined disability`)

§ `Tests of what was read from where`

-- The defect: both limbs were read from official instruments.
#ASSERT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 1יג(ד)(2) to NII s 223א, a suspended permit`)
-- The two controls in the same sentence: limb (b) is official (the same page), limb (a) is the consolidation only, so not both.
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 1יג(ד)(2) to NII s 1, the retirement age`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 1יג(ד)(2) to NII s 223, the nursing benefit`))
#ASSERT (`reference: s 1יג(ד)(2) to NII s 1, the retirement age`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 1יג(ד)(2) to NII s 223, the nursing benefit`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
-- The control in s 2(א1)(1): both limbs are the consolidations only.
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 2(א1)(1) to NII s 398(א2)(5), a person with a determined disability`))
#ASSERT (`reference: s 2(א1)(1) to NII s 398(א2)(5), a person with a determined disability`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`

§ `Tests of what the two descriptions of the defect say`

-- What the citing words say it points at, and what the target is, as the page images show them.
#ASSERT (`reference: s 1יג(ד)(2) to NII s 223א, a suspended permit`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `the definition of a suspended permit`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 1יג(ד)(2) to NII s 223א, a suspended permit`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `a definition that was deleted, so that the section prints no text for the term`

§ `Tests of the day the target was deleted`

-- Sefer HaChukim 2713 p. 527, s 25(ב): the deletion in s 23(2) commences on 23 Cheshvan 5779 = 1 November 2018.
#ASSERT `the target stands in the official text on` (`reference: s 1יג(ד)(2) to NII s 223א, a suspended permit`) (Date 1 11 2018) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the target stands in the official text on` (`reference: s 1יג(ד)(2) to NII s 223א, a suspended permit`) (Date 2 11 2018) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the target stands in the official text on` (`reference: s 1יג(ד)(2) to NII s 223א, a suspended permit`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The day before: no source held says whether or when the definition was added, so NOTHING (fork D1 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `the target stands in the official text on` (`reference: s 1יג(ד)(2) to NII s 223א, a suspended permit`) (Date 31 10 2018) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the target stands in the official text on` (`reference: s 1יג(ד)(2) to NII s 223א, a suspended permit`) (Date 6 8 2013) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A control has no recorded deletion: NOTHING on any day, which is not a statement that the target stands.
#ASSERT `the target stands in the official text on` (`reference: s 1יג(ד)(2) to NII s 1, the retirement age`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
